---

IMPORTANT DESIGN PRINCIPLE

Ostra is NOT supposed to be just a chat UI.

The long-term architecture is:

Model = brain

Agent runtime = decision/execution layer

Tools = actions

Memory = persistent knowledge

Scheduler = autonomy

Website = communication/control interface

For v0, only implement:

Model + basic runtime + website communication.

But structure the code so the rest can be added cleanly.

---

DEPLOYMENT

The project must deploy successfully on Vercel.

Before finishing:

1. install dependencies
2. run lint/type checks
3. run production build
4. fix all build errors
5. verify API routes
6. verify mock mode
7. verify mobile layout
8. verify environment variables
9. provide deployment instructions

Do not leave placeholder code that breaks the build.

---

DEFINITION OF DONE

The task is complete only when:

- the Ostra website loads
- the chat interface works
- user can send a message
- mock Ostra responds
- conversation persists locally
- /api/health works
- HTTP model provider is implemented
- model URL is configurable
- secrets remain server-side
- mobile layout works
- production build succeeds
- Vercel deployment is supported

Do not over-engineer the project.

Build a clean foundation for the next Ostra phase.
